te 0.18 at time of check), running in us-east, us-west, and eu-west. v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy. Most recent healthy release was v2.3.0. Rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west); rollout verified. v2.3.1 and v2.3.1-rc are marked unhealthy and should not be redeployed until root cause is fixed.", "confidence": 0.9, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The rollout is verified.\n\n- **Why v2.3.0:** v2.3.1 and v2.3.1-rc are both marked unhealthy. v2.3.0 is the most recent release marked healthy.\n- **Before the rollback:** v2.3.1 was running in all regions, with a 0.18 error rate.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api, which paged the on-call engineer. The summary describes the rollback and notes that v2.3.1 and v2.3.1-rc should not be redeployed until the root cause is fixed.\n\nI haven't checked the live error rate since the rollback, so it's worth confirming that checkout-api's health has recovered.", "type": "text"}]}]}